This project is a from-scratch trainer for Stockfish 16.1 "Small" networks.
It contains original Rust and Python code written for this project, plus
reference/derived behaviour from the following GPL projects:

1. Stockfish
   Source:  https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish (tag sf_16.1)
   License: GNU GPL v3.0
   Copyright: The Stockfish developers
   Use: architecture constants, HalfKAv2_hm feature layout, layer stack and
        PSQT bucket rules, integer inference/quantization and .nnue file
        serialization. No Stockfish source is compiled or linked.

2. nnue-pytorch
   Source:  https://github.com/official-stockfish/nnue-pytorch
            (commit 2db3787d2e36f7142ea4d0e307b502dda4095cd9)
   License: GNU GPL v3.0
   Copyright: The Stockfish developers
   Use: float training semantics (pairwise product, PSQT initialisation,
        win-rate loss, weight clipping) and serialization layout.

3. sfbinpack
   Source:  https://github.com/Disservin/binpack-rust
   License: GNU GPL v3.0
   Copyright: Disservin and contributors
   Use: reading real Stockfish .binpack files and position representation.

4. pyo3 / numpy-rs / ndarray / crossbeam-channel / thiserror
   Licenses: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (see each crate)
   Use: Rust <-> Python bindings and concurrency.

